<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">resources</ansi>

Some rooms provide something your company can use. <ansi fg="command">look</ansi> names it on a
line that starts with "Here:", and the web client's map marks the room with
a small coloured dot in the corner of its tile (hover over a room to read
what it offers). Turn the dots off under the map's settings button.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the markers mean</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Fresh water</ansi> (blue)
  A source you can drink from and fill a container at. It costs nothing
  and takes no game time.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Forage</ansi> (green)
  A camp rest that finishes here brings back one more find than usual
  (<ansi fg="command">help forage</ansi>). Where a zone has nothing to find, there is nothing extra.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Shelter</ansi> (tan)
  A roof, a cave, or thick walls. A camp rest started here loses only half of
  what bad weather would take from it: recovery moves halfway from the
  weather's figure toward a full rest (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>). An inn stay is not changed.

Forage and shelter only matter to a camp rest, so they are marked only in
rooms where you can make camp (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>).

  <ansi fg="yellow">Herbs</ansi> (teal), <ansi fg="yellow">Firewood</ansi> (orange), <ansi fg="yellow">Fishing</ansi> (cyan), <ansi fg="yellow">Game</ansi> (red)
  Things your company can gather: <ansi fg="command">gather herbs</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">gather firewood</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">fish</ansi> and
  <ansi fg="command">hunt</ansi>. Each room holds only so much, and a resource that has been picked
  clean says "(picked clean)" on the "Here:" line and is drawn hollow with
  a slash on the map until it grows back (<ansi fg="command">help gathering</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Water commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">drink water</ansi>  or  <ansi fg="command">drink source</ansi>
  Drinks from the water here: the same 40 Thirst as one glug of a
  waterskin, and the Hydrated buff. Add a companion's name to water them
  instead: <ansi fg="command">drink water tamsin</ansi>. Away from a source, <ansi fg="command">drink source</ansi> says there is
  none, and <ansi fg="command">drink water</ansi> keeps its old meaning, drinking a water item you carry.

  <ansi fg="command">fill</ansi>
  Fills every refillable container in your pack (a waterskin) back to full.
  A waterskin is used up with its last glug, so fill it before it runs dry.

  <ansi fg="command">fill waterskin</ansi>
  Fills just that one.

  <ansi fg="command">company fill</ansi>
  Fills the refillable containers your whole company carries: your
  pack, each companion with you, and the cargo.

  <ansi fg="command">company drink</ansi>
  At a water source, everyone who is thirsty drinks from the source until
  they are no longer thirsty, without using up any supplies.

None of these work during a battle (<ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help gathering</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help drink</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help forage</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help company meal</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>.
